{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And the dismantling of the Tabernacle.</b> Once the banner of Judah set out, Aaron and his sons would enter and take down the curtain and cover the Ark with it, as it says: ״וּבָא אַהֲרֹן וּבָנָיו בִּנְסֹעַ הַמַּחֲנֶה״ (Numbers 4). And the sons of Gershon and the sons of Merari would dismantle the Tabernacle and load it onto the wagons, while the Ark and the sacred utensils carried by the sons of Kohath would stand covered and placed on their poles until the banner of the camp of Reuben set out — and only then ״וְנָסְעוּ הַקְּהָתִים״ (see Tanhuma)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:10.531759584Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}